    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Brady is delighted to present this exceptional 5-bedroom detached residence to the market. Situated on a beautifully maintained and private c. 1-acre site, this stunning family home is presented in excellent condition throughout and offers bright, spacious, and well-proportioned accommodation extending to approximately 188 sq. metres 2024 sq. ft..\nUpon entering, you are welcomed by a bright and spacious entrance hall featuring attractive wood flooring, a large window allowing for an abundance of natural light, a feature staircase, pine ceiling, and recessed lighting, creating a warm and inviting first impression.\nThe generous living room is beautifully appointed with elegant coving and a multi-fuel burning stove with back boiler, providing both comfort and efficiency. Double doors lead through to the conservatory, creating a wonderful flow between the living spaces and offering an ideal area for relaxation and entertaining.\nThe heart of the home is the beautiful oak fitted kitchen, offering ample storage and workspace. A practical utility room, plumbed for a washing machine, is conveniently located just off the kitchen.\nThe ground floor bedroom also benefits from a Jack and Jill-style bathroom/ensuite, providing flexibility and convenience for family living and guests alike.\nUpstairs, the property boasts four well-proportioned bedrooms together with a fully tiled family bathroom\n\nOutside\nThe residence is set on a superbly landscaped and sheltered c. 1-acre site with mature gardens and ample outdoor space. A large detached garage provides excellent storage and workshop facilities and includes a W.C. and a first-floor area that offers excellent potential for conversion, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nLocation\nIdeally located in the beautiful countryside of Monasterboice, the property enjoys the perfect balance of rural living and convenience. Drogheda town centre is just 15 minutes away, while the M1 motorway can be reached in approximately 5 minutes, providing easy access to Dublin, Belfast, and beyond.\nA range of local amenities are nearby, including a primary school, Donegan's Bar & Restaurant, the local GAA club, and the thriving town of Dunleer.\nViewing of this outstanding family home is highly recommended."
      },
